{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-psa-109-1","title":"Psalms 109:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":109,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":109,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 David, complaining of his slanderous enemies, under the person of Judas devotes them. 16 He shews their sin. 21 Complaining of his own misery, he prays for help. 29 He promises thankfulness.</p>\n<p>A.M. 2942. B.C. 1062. (Title.)It is generally supposed that this Psalm was composed by David, when persecuted by Saul, who was rendered more implacable by the base and malicious calumnies of Doeg and others; though some are of opinion, that it was written when David fled from Absalom, and that Ahithophel, rather than Doeg, is the typical person against whom it is principally directed.</p>\n<p>Hold. 28:1; 35:22,23; 83:1; Isa 42:14 O God. 118:28; Ex 15:2; De 10:21; Jer 17:14</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-109-2","title":"Psalms 109:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":109,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":109,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>the mouth. 31:13,18; 64:3,4; 140:3; 2Sa 15:3-8; 17:1; Pr 15:28; Mt 26:59-62 of the deceitful. Heb. of deceit. are opened. Heb. haveopened themselves. with. 120:3; Pr 6:17; 12:19; Jer 9:3,5; Ac 6:13</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-109-3","title":"Psalms 109:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":109,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":109,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>compassed. 17:11; 22:12; 88:17; 2Sa 16:7,8; Ho 11:12 fought. 35:7,20; 59:3,4; 69:4; 1Sa 19:4,5; 26:18; 2Sa 15:12; Joh 15:24,25</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-109-4","title":"Psalms 109:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":109,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":109,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>For my. 35:7,12; 38:20; 2Sa 13:39; Joh 10:32; 2Co 12:15 but I. 55:16,17; 69:12,13; 2Sa 15:31,32; Da 6:10; Lu 6:11,12; 23:34</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-109-5","title":"Psalms 109:5","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":109,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":109,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>they. 35:7-12; Ge 44:4; Pr 17:13 hatred. 55:12-15; 2Sa 15:12,31; Mr 14:44,45; Lu 6:16; 22:47,48; Joh 13:18</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-109-6","title":"Psalms 109:6","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":109,"verseStart":6,"chapterEnd":109,"verseEnd":6},"content":"<p>Set thou.Dr. Sykes, Michaelis, and others, contend that these imprecations are those of David's enemies against himself; and they would render, \"Set, say they, a wicked,\" etc: but this is rendered highly improbable by the 8th verse being applied by St. Peter to the traitor Judas, of whom David was certainly not a type. (See ver. 20.) Bp. Horsley and others, however, render the verbs in the future tense, the first verb alone being in the imperative; justly considering the Psalmist as merely uttering prophetic denunciations of God's displeasure against sinners.</p>\n<p>Mt 27:4 and let. Zec 3:1; Joh 13:2,27 Satan. or, an adversary. Mt 5:25</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-109-7","title":"Psalms 109:7","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":109,"verseStart":7,"chapterEnd":109,"verseEnd":7},"content":"<p>be condemned. Heb. go out guilty, or wicked. Ro 3:19; Ga 3:10 and let. 2Sa 15:7,8; Pr 15:8; 21:27; 28:9; Isa 1:15; 66:3; Mt 23:14</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-109-8","title":"Psalms 109:8","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":109,"verseStart":8,"chapterEnd":109,"verseEnd":8},"content":"<p>his days. 55:23; Mt 27:5 another. Ac 1:16-26 office. or, charge.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-109-9","title":"Psalms 109:9","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":109,"verseStart":9,"chapterEnd":109,"verseEnd":9},"content":"<p>Ex 22:24; Jer 18:21; La 5:3</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-109-10","title":"Psalms 109:10","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":109,"verseStart":10,"chapterEnd":109,"verseEnd":10},"content":"<p>37:25; Ge 4:12-14; 2Sa 3:29; 2Ki 5:27; Job 24:8-12; 30:3-9 Isa 16:2</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-109-11","title":"Psalms 109:11","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":109,"verseStart":11,"chapterEnd":109,"verseEnd":11},"content":"<p>extortioner. Job 5:5; 18:9-19; 20:18 strangers. De 28:29,33,34,50,51; Jud 6:3-6</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-109-12","title":"Psalms 109:12","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":109,"verseStart":12,"chapterEnd":109,"verseEnd":12},"content":"<p>none. Isa 27:11; Lu 6:38; Jas 2:13 favour. 137:8,9; Isa 13:18; Mt 27:25; Lu 11:50,51</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-109-13","title":"Psalms 109:13","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":109,"verseStart":13,"chapterEnd":109,"verseEnd":13},"content":"<p>Let his. 37:28; 1Sa 2:31-33; 3:13; 2Ki 10:10,11; Job 18:19; Isa 14:20-22 Jer 22:30 their name. De 9:14; 25:19; 29:20; Pr 10:7</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-109-14","title":"Psalms 109:14","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":109,"verseStart":14,"chapterEnd":109,"verseEnd":14},"content":"<p>Let the. Ex 20:5; Le 26:39; 2Sa 3:29; 21:1,8,9; Mt 23:31-36 let not. 2Ki 8:27; 9:27; 10:13,14; 11:1; 2Ch 22:3,4 blotted. Ne 4:5; Isa 43:25; Jer 18:23</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-109-15","title":"Psalms 109:15","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":109,"verseStart":15,"chapterEnd":109,"verseEnd":15},"content":"<p>before. 51:9; 90:8; De 32:34; Jer 2:22; Ho 7:2; Am 8:7 cut off. 13; 34:16; Job 18:17; Isa 65:15</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-109-16","title":"Psalms 109:16","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":109,"verseStart":16,"chapterEnd":109,"verseEnd":16},"content":"<p>he remembered. 2Sa 17:1,2; Mt 5:7; 18:33-35; Jas 2:13 persecuted. 10:2,14; Ge 42:21; Job 19:2,3,21,22; Mt 27:35-46 slay. 34:18; 69:20-29; 2Sa 16:11,12; Mr 14:34-36</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-109-17","title":"Psalms 109:17","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":109,"verseStart":17,"chapterEnd":109,"verseEnd":17},"content":"<p>52:4,5; 59:12,13; Pr 14:14; Eze 35:6; Mt 7:2; 2Th 2:10,11 Re 16:6</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-109-18","title":"Psalms 109:18","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":109,"verseStart":18,"chapterEnd":109,"verseEnd":18},"content":"<p>As he. 73:6; Job 29:14; Col 3:8,12; 1Pe 5:5 so let. Nu 5:22,27; Job 20:12-16,20-23; Mt 26:24; 27:3-5; Ac 1:18,25 into his bowels. Heb. within him.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-109-19","title":"Psalms 109:19","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":109,"verseStart":19,"chapterEnd":109,"verseEnd":19},"content":"<p>as the garment. 18,29; 35:26; 132:18</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-109-20","title":"Psalms 109:20","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":109,"verseStart":20,"chapterEnd":109,"verseEnd":20},"content":"<p>Let this. 2:5,6,12; 21:8-12; 40:14,15; 110:1,5,6; 2Sa 17:23; 18:32; 1Ki 2:44 Lu 19:27; 1Th 2:15,16 them. Mt 11:19; 12:24; 26:66,67; Mr 9:39; 1Co 12:3</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-109-21","title":"Psalms 109:21","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":109,"verseStart":21,"chapterEnd":109,"verseEnd":21},"content":"<p>But do. 25:11; 31:3; 69:29; 79:9,10; 143:11,12; Joh 17:1; Php 2:8-11 thy mercy. 36:7-9; 63:3; 86:5,15</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-109-22","title":"Psalms 109:22","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":109,"verseStart":22,"chapterEnd":109,"verseEnd":22},"content":"<p>For I. 22:6; 40:17; 86:1; 102:17-20; Mt 8:20; 2Co 8:9 and my. 16; 88:15,16; 102:4; 2Ki 4:27; Job 6:4; Isa 53:3; Lu 22:44 Joh 12:27</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-109-23","title":"Psalms 109:23","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":109,"verseStart":23,"chapterEnd":109,"verseEnd":23},"content":"<p>gone. 102:11; 144:4; 1Ch 29:15; Job 14:2; Ec 6:12; 8:13; Jas 4:14 I am tossed. 102:10; Ex 10:13,19</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-109-24","title":"Psalms 109:24","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":109,"verseStart":24,"chapterEnd":109,"verseEnd":24},"content":"<p>knees. 22:14; 35:13,14; 69:10; Mt 4:2; 2Co 11:27; Heb 12:12 my flesh. 32:3,4; 38:5-8; 102:4,5; Job 19:20</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-109-25","title":"Psalms 109:25","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":109,"verseStart":25,"chapterEnd":109,"verseEnd":25},"content":"<p>a reproach. 31:11-13; 35:15,16; 69:9-12,19,20; Ro 15:3; Heb 12:2; 13:13 when they. 22:6,7; Job 16:4; Isa 37:22; Mt 27:39,40</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-109-26","title":"Psalms 109:26","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":109,"verseStart":26,"chapterEnd":109,"verseEnd":26},"content":"<p>Help. 40:12; 119:86; Heb 5:7 save me. 57:1; 69:13,16</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-109-27","title":"Psalms 109:27","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":109,"verseStart":27,"chapterEnd":109,"verseEnd":27},"content":"<p>17:13,14; 64:8,9; 126:2; Ex 8:19; Nu 16:28-30; 1Sa 17:46,47 1Ki 18:36,37; Job 37:7; Ac 2:32-36; 4:16</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-109-28","title":"Psalms 109:28","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":109,"verseStart":28,"chapterEnd":109,"verseEnd":28},"content":"<p>Let them. 17; Nu 22:12; 23:20,23; 2Sa 16:10-13 but let. Isa 65:13-16; Joh 16:22; Heb 12:2</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-109-29","title":"Psalms 109:29","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":109,"verseStart":29,"chapterEnd":109,"verseEnd":29},"content":"<p>be clothed. 17-19; 6:10; 35:26; 132:18; 140:9; Jer 20:11; Da 12:2; Mic 7:10</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-109-30","title":"Psalms 109:30","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":109,"verseStart":30,"chapterEnd":109,"verseEnd":30},"content":"<p>greatly. 7:17; 9:1; 22:22,25; 71:22,23; 108:1-3 I will praise. 22:22-25; 35:18; 107:32; 111:1; 116:12-18; 138:1,4; Heb 2:12</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-109-31","title":"Psalms 109:31","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":109,"verseStart":31,"chapterEnd":109,"verseEnd":31},"content":"<p>For he. 16:8; 73:23; 110:5; 121:5 poor. 16; 68:5; 72:4,12,13; 140:12 to save. 10:14; Ex 22:22-24; Pr 22:22,23; Ec 5:8; Isa 54:17; Ac 4:10-12 5:30,31 those that condemn. Heb. the judges of.</p>"}]}